(LST2-71: LANGUAGE.md:3429-3430: English's zip marker, `respectively`, is
 an ordinary identifier in Vox, not parsed as a marker. Both halves hold:
 it is accepted as a variable name, and a sentence using it as a marker
 does not compile. Until vox #290 the manual called it "reserved", which
 it never was; see Discrepancy 9, resolved. Re-run on vox cb407f8.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-71.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   4
   a zip marker sentence does not compile: see D9.vox
)
a number called respectively is 4.
print respectively.
print "a zip marker sentence does not compile: see D9.vox".
